From: brainux-pw-a9300
Subject: [PATCH] iio: adc: mxs-lradc-adc: only clear our own interrupt flags

LRADC_CTRL1 holds the interrupt flags of all eight virtual channels and is
shared with the touchscreen driver, which uses channels 6 and 7. The ADC
interrupt handler cleared every flag in it. When an ADC read finished
while a touchscreen conversion was pending, the touchscreen never saw its
interrupt and stayed "touched" for good: no more touch events until the
input device was closed by every user.

Only look at and clear the flags of the channels this driver uses:
channel 0 for single reads, buffer_vchans in buffered mode.

Seen on Brain PW-A9300 with the sub-LCD touch panel and a 10 s ADC poll.

Checked on PW-A9300 together with the mxs-lradc-ts change: 180 s of
back-to-back ADC reads (6164, no errors) while tapping and dragging on
the sub-LCD; every touch was released and the touch-detect wait state
was back afterwards.

diff --git a/drivers/iio/adc/mxs-lradc-adc.c b/drivers/iio/adc/mxs-lradc-adc.c
index a50f39143..53288c2f9 100644
--- a/drivers/iio/adc/mxs-lradc-adc.c
+++ b/drivers/iio/adc/mxs-lradc-adc.c
@@ -388,8 +388,15 @@ static irqreturn_t mxs_lradc_adc_handle_irq(int irq, void *data)
 	struct mxs_lradc *lradc = adc->lradc;
 	unsigned long reg = readl(adc->base + LRADC_CTRL1);
 	unsigned long flags;
+	/*
+	 * LRADC_CTRL1 is shared with the touchscreen: only look at and clear
+	 * the flags of our own virtual channels, or a touchscreen conversion
+	 * can lose its interrupt and the touchscreen stops.
+	 */
+	u32 own = iio_buffer_enabled(iio) ? lradc->buffer_vchans :
+					      LRADC_CTRL1_LRADC_IRQ(0);
 
-	if (!(reg & mxs_lradc_irq_mask(lradc)))
+	if (!(reg & own))
 		return IRQ_NONE;
 
 	if (iio_buffer_enabled(iio)) {
@@ -402,8 +409,7 @@ static irqreturn_t mxs_lradc_adc_handle_irq(int irq, void *data)
 		complete(&adc->completion);
 	}
 
-	writel(reg & mxs_lradc_irq_mask(lradc),
-	       adc->base + LRADC_CTRL1 + STMP_OFFSET_REG_CLR);
+	writel(reg & own, adc->base + LRADC_CTRL1 + STMP_OFFSET_REG_CLR);
 
 	return IRQ_HANDLED;
 }
